        "y2": 995.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9371151924133301,
      "reading_order": 6,
      "text": "1. 5th period is called second long period. Ele-\nments with atomic numbers from 37 to 54 are\nin 5th period.\n\nHence, the correct option is (c)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_006",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 234.0,
        "y1": 1017.0,
        "x2": 1136.0,
        "y2": 1141.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9124970436096191,
      "reading_order": 7,
      "text": "2. Reducing property is maximum for caesium.\nHence, the correct option is (c)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_007",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 236.0,
        "y1": 1163.0,
        "x2": 1163.0,
        "y2": 1411.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9446043372154236,
      "reading_order": 8,
      "text": "3. The three triads which obey Dobereiner’s Law\nof Triads are $(\\mathrm{}_{20}\\mathrm{Ca}, \\mathrm{}_{38}\\mathrm{Sr}, \\mathrm{}_{56}\\mathrm{Ba})$, $(\\mathrm{}_3\\mathrm{Li}, \\mathrm{}_{11}\\mathrm{Na}, \\mathrm{}_{19}\\mathrm{K})$\nand $(\\mathrm{}_{17}\\mathrm{Cl}, \\mathrm{}_{35}\\mathrm{Br}, \\mathrm{}_{53}\\mathrm{I})$.\nHence, the correct option is (d)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_008",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 234.0,
        "y1": 1433.0,
        "x2": 1142.0,
        "y2": 1761.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9456860423088074,
      "reading_order": 9,
      "text": "4. A → Na; Na has less tendency to form cation.\nB → Ar; Ar has zero electron affinity.\nC → Cl; Cl has good oxidizing property.\nD → Rb; Rb has minimum ionization energy.\nHence, the correct option is (d)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_009",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 234.0,
        "y1": 1780.0,
        "x2": 1137.0,
        "y2": 2156.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9377214908599854,
      "reading_order": 10,
      "text": "5. A belongs to IA group.\nB belongs to II-A group.\nC belongs to VII-A group.\nD belongs to VI-A/IV-A/V-A groups.\n$\\therefore$ The correct order of atomic sizes is CDBA.\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_010",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 233.0,
        "y1": 2175.0,
        "x2": 1143.0,
        "y2": 2608.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "table",
      "confidence": 0.9451916217803955,
      "reading_order": 11,
      "text": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Electronic<br/>Configuration</th>\n<th>Group</th>\n<th>Type of<br/>Element</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>2, 8, 8, 1</td>\n<td>I-A</td>\n<td>Alkali Metal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2, 8, 18, 8, 2</td>\n<td>II-A</td>\n<td>Alkaline earth<br/>metal</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2, 8, 18, 18, 7</td>\n<td>VII-A</td>\n<td>Halogen</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2, 8, 18, 6</td>\n<td>VI-A</td>\n<td>Chalcogen</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_011",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 297.0,
        "y1": 2624.0,
        "x2": 882.0,
        "y2": 2676.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "footnote",
      "confidence": 0.6727229952812195,
      "reading_order": 12,
      "text": "Hence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_012",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 234.0,
        "y1": 2706.0,
        "x2": 1173.0,
        "y2": 2815.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9008612036705017,
      "reading_order": 13,
      "text": "7. $\\mathrm{Na}^+$ ion possesses a stable octet configuration.\nHence, the second I.P of $\\mathrm{Na}^{+1}$ is greater than"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_013",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1343.0,
        "y1": 292.0,
        "x2": 1933.0,
        "y2": 421.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.7941502332687378,
      "reading_order": 14,
      "text": "that of $\\mathrm{Mg}^{+1}$.\n\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_014",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1288.0,
        "y1": 440.0,
        "x2": 2220.0,
        "y2": 729.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9398313760757446,
      "reading_order": 15,
      "text": "8. With increase in number of electrons in the\nspecies, the repulsive force increases. Hence,\nenergy absorbed is more than energy released\nduring the addition of second electron.\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_015",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1285.0,
        "y1": 757.0,
        "x2": 2220.0,
        "y2": 1137.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9250831007957458,
      "reading_order": 16,
      "text": "9. Due to stable electronic configuration of N, it\npossesses high I.P value than that of C.\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{X} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{C}$\n$\\mathrm{Y} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{N}$\n$\\mathrm{Z} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{O}$\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_016",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1266.0,
        "y1": 1164.0,
        "x2": 2219.0,
        "y2": 1399.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9392988085746765,
      "reading_order": 17,
      "text": "10. Electronic configuration of X is 2, 8, 18, and 6.\nThe difference in the number of electrons pres-\nent between the last shell and first shell is 4.\nHence, the correct option is (b)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_017",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1267.0,
        "y1": 1428.0,
        "x2": 2217.0,
        "y2": 1608.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9213933348655701,
      "reading_order": 18,
      "text": "11. Across the period, the atomic sizes decrease up\nto VII-A group and then increase.\nHence, the correct option is (b)"
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_018",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1268.0,
        "y1": 1635.0,
        "x2": 2220.0,
        "y2": 1921.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9362021088600159,
      "reading_order": 19,
      "text": "12. X, Y, and Z are Ca, Sr, and Ba, respectively.\nDown the group oxidizing property decreases\nand reducing property increases. Hence, Ba is\ngood reducing agent.\n\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_019",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1265.0,
        "y1": 1953.0,
        "x2": 2221.0,
        "y2": 2242.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9284912347793579,
      "reading_order": 20,
      "text": "13. In case of cation, effective nuclear charge is\nmore as against the corresponding neutral\natom. Hence, the size of the atom is greater\nthan cation. It is reverse in case of anions.\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_020",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1264.0,
        "y1": 2284.0,
        "x2": 2097.0,
        "y2": 2542.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.8842037320137024,
      "reading_order": 21,
      "text": "14. X → S, B → O, D → Se\nA → P, C → Cl\nSelenium is least non-metallic in nature.\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    },
    {
      "block_id": "20260312_53230d52-1143-496b-ac7c-3377ccdd9795_3_block_021",
      "coordinates": {
        "x1": 1266.0,
        "y1": 2579.0,
        "x2": 2222.0,
        "y2": 2816.0
      },
      "layout_tag": "paragraph",
      "confidence": 0.9131075143814087,
      "reading_order": 22,
      "text": "15. Phosphorus is used for manufacture of match\nsticks. Phosphorus belongs to the third period\nand V-A group.\nHence, the correct option is (a)."
    }
